; test_data_gen — the `gen` half of `(buffer … :file …)`.
;
; A data WASM has two shapes and the exports decide which. With `l` (byte
; length) and `s` (where those bytes sit in the module's memory) alone, the
; module is a container: the compiler reads its data segments at build time and
; ships the bytes, nothing else (examples/test_data_pass.sjon). Export a `gen`
; function beside them and the module becomes a program: it is embedded whole,
; the runtime calls `gen` once when the buffer is created, and `gen` returns the
; pointer its bytes were written to.
;
; assets/gen_ramp.wasm takes the second shape and carries NO data segment at
; all — read statically it is twelve zero bytes. `gen` computes i * 0.5 for
; i in 0..2, so a canvas that is azure (0, 0.5, 1) is one where the runtime ran
; the module, and a BLACK canvas is one where it did not. That is the whole
; assertion, and nothing else in the corpus was making it: every other `:file`
; document takes the container shape.
;
; `s` is 16 here rather than 0, which is the other thing this fixture pins. `s`
; addresses the MODULE's memory; the GPU buffer is exactly `l` bytes long and is
; always written from 0. The two offsets meet in `write_buffer_from_wasm`, whose
; frozen operand (docs/abi.md §6, `buffer_off`) is the destination — so passing
; `s` there wrote past the end of a buffer that had no room for it, silently
; correct for every fixture that had `s` = 0 and wrong for the first one that
; did not. §435 found the same shape of defect one operand to the left.
;
; The native backend stubs the three `[wasm]` opcodes, so this document renders
; black under `--frame`; its gate is the frozen MockGPU trace
; (tests/zig/golden/test_data_gen.trace), which pins the operands, and the
; browser, which pins the pixels.

; No `:size`: `l` is the length. The bind group leaves `:layout` out and is
; derived from the one pipeline that binds it.
(buffer :name ramp :file "assets/gen_ramp.wasm" :usage [storage copy-dst])

(shader-module :name code :code """
@group(0) @binding(0) var<storage, read> ramp: array<f32>;

@vertex fn vs(@builtin(vertex_index) i: u32) -> @builtin(position) vec4f {
  let x = f32(i & 1u) * 4.0 - 1.0;
  let y = f32((i >> 1u) & 1u) * 4.0 - 1.0;
  return vec4f(x, y, 0, 1);
}

@fragment fn fs() -> @location(0) vec4f {
  return vec4f(ramp[0], ramp[1], ramp[2], 1.0);
}
""")

(render-pipeline :name pipe :layout auto
  (vertex :module code :entry vs)
  (fragment :module code :entry fs
    (color-target :format preferred-canvas-format)))

(bind-group :name bg :group 0
  (entry :binding 0 :buffer ramp))

(render-pass :name draw :pipeline pipe :bind-groups [bg]
  (color-attachment :view context-current-texture :clear-value [0 0 0 1]
    :load-op clear :store-op store)
  (draw :vertex-count 3))

(frame :name main :perform [draw])
